# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Reading-assistant secrets. .env.local holds the Hermes API_SERVER_KEY, which
# grants the agent's full toolset (including terminal) - it must NEVER be
# committed or served. Covered by *.local above; named here so nobody "tidies"
# that pattern away.
.env.local
.env

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Serving copies of the real books (masters live in the MEGA archive).
# Regenerate with: python tools/sync_library.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# public/Prime Books/ is a 30 GB WORKING MIRROR of the MEGA masters. It must
# NEVER be committed or deployed:
#   * PDF/Input holds third-party publisher material (Cambridge, Pearson,
#     Collins syllabuses) kept for SCOPE ONLY. Publishing it is a copyright
#     breach, and it is reachable by URL the moment it lands in public/.
#   * it carries FEEDBACK.docx, WORKSTATION/ build exhaust and _superseded_*
#     editions that no reader should see.
#   * Vercel would refuse the deployment long before that anyway.
# The site serves a SELECTED, web-optimised subset built by tools/sync_library.py.
public/Prime Books/
public/PROJECT-HUB/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The old flat root copies and public/books/ are superseded by public/library/
# + library.json (written by tools/sync_library.py). public/books/ was deleted
# 2026-08-14, together with public/subjects/ and public/covers/.
public/*.pdf
copy-books.sh

# The old flat-root served copies (public/books/, public/books-manifest.json) are
# superseded by public/library/ + library.json, written by tools/sync_library.py.
# public/library/ IS deployed (it is what the flipbook fetches); the local variant
# carries absolute MEGA paths and must never ship.
public/library.local.json

# Python bytecode. tools/__pycache__/webopt_pdf.cpython-311.pyc was committed by
# accident and showed up as a modified file on every sync run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Verification-harness scratch output
uiauth.log
*.tmp.js

# Manifest variant carrying absolute MEGA paths: local authoring only, must
# never deploy (it would publish the folder layout of the masters).
# (Also listed above with the other served-copy rules; both entries agree.)
work/
public/inputs/y08-humanities - input.pdf
public/library/y08-humanities/book.pdf
dist/
.venv

# BookVault print packs are DERIVED from library/<slug>/book.pdf by
# tools/make_bookvault_files.py: a PDF/X interior plus a 300 DPI cover wrap,
# 10-15 MB per title. 123 titles of that is ~1.7 GB the repo does not need, so
# only the small record (build.json) and the upload sheet are tracked - the
# deployed site can still show the checks, and the files themselves are built
# on demand and served through the live tunnel.
public/library/*/bookvault/*.pdf
public/library/*/bookvault/*.png

# local-only pre-normalisation copies of the input spreadsheets (git history is the real backup)
public/inputs/.backup-original/
